# The console, gated when there is a gate -- every door asks, once a
# factor exists to ask for.
#
# THIS USED TO BE AN AUTOLOGIN SHELL, and the file that shipped it said
# plainly when that had to end: "WHEN IT HAS BEEN PROVEN, the console
# service's own getty line is the thing to change." veron-login is now
# proven on hardware -- Enter with the factor present gives a shell,
# without it a refusal that prints its reason -- so the spare-console hole
# closes. A lock screen beside an unauthenticated VT is decoration: the
# session layer's one invariant is COMPLETE MEDIATION, no input path into
# a session that does not ask.
#
# scripts/console-or-login IS THE -l TARGET, NOT veron-login DIRECTLY,
# because a machine with nothing enrolled has no factor to ask for: the
# live image and a fresh install must land in a shell, and a login prompt
# that cannot be satisfied is a machine you reinstall. The chooser execs
# veron-login when a keyfile slot is enrolled and the open shell when not
# -- the same conditional the boot gate applies, read from the same file.
#
# THE ESCAPE HATCH MOVES TO THE BOOT, WHERE IT ALWAYS REALLY WAS. A person
# locked out (lost factor) recovers with physical access via GRUB
# `rdinit=/bin/busybox sh` -- reboot-required, documented, honest. On a
# machine with no disk encryption that hatch is unavoidable anyway;
# closing the live VT while naming the physical one is the honest shape.
type = process
command = /bin/busybox getty -n -l /etc/dinit.d/scripts/console-or-login 115200 ttyAMA0
run-as = veron
restart = true
depends-on = early-filesystems
depends-on = device-nodes
